  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Alma",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 53,
    "summary": "The Lamanite prisoners are used to fortify the city Bountiful—Dissensions among the Nephites give rise to Lamanite victories—Helaman takes command of the two thousand stripling sons of the people of Ammon. About 64–63 B.C.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that they did set guards over the prisoners of the Lamanites, and did compel them to go forth and bury their dead, yea, and also the dead of the Nephites who were slain; and Moroni placed men over them to guard them while they should perform their labors.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 53:1",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 53,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And Moroni went to the city of Mulek with Lehi, and took command of the city and gave it unto Lehi. Now behold, this Lehi was a man who had been with Moroni in the more part of all his battles; and he was a man like unto Moroni, and they rejoiced in each other’s safety; yea, they were beloved by each other, and also beloved by all the people of Nephi.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 211,
            "end": 215,
            "text": "Alma 48:17."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 48:17.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 48:17",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 48,
                    "end": 48,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 17,
                        "end": 17
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 53:2",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 53,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that after the Lamanites had finished burying their dead and also the dead of the Nephites, they were marched back into the land Bountiful; and Teancum, by the orders of Moroni, caused that they should commence laboring in digging a ditch round about the land, or the city, Bountiful.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 243,
            "end": 250,
            "text": "Alma 52:6."
          },
          {
            "start": 294,
            "end": 303,
            "text": "Alma 52:9 (9, 17, 27); 63:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 52:6.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 52:6",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 52,
                    "end": 52,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 6,
                        "end": 6
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 53:3",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 53,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And he caused that they should build a breastwork of timbers upon the inner bank of the ditch; and they cast up dirt out of the ditch against the breastwork of timbers; and thus they did cause the Lamanites to labor until they had encircled the city of Bountiful round about with a strong wall of timbers and earth, to an exceeding height.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "Alma 50:2 (2–3)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 53:4",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 53,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And this city became an exceeding stronghold ever after; and in this city they did guard the prisoners of the Lamanites; yea, even within a wall which they had caused them to build with their own hands. Now Moroni was compelled to cause the Lamanites to labor, because it was easy to guard them while at their labor; and he desired all his forces when he should make an attack upon the Lamanites.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 175,
            "end": 180,
            "text": "Alma 55:25 (25–26)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 53:5",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 53,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that Moroni had thus gained a victory over one of the greatest of the armies of the Lamanites, and had obtained possession of the city of Mulek, which was one of the strongest holds of the Lamanites in the land of Nephi; and thus he had also built a stronghold to retain his prisoners.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 158,
            "end": 163,
            "text": "Alma 51:26; 52:22."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 51:26; 52:22.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 51:26; 52:22",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 51,
                    "end": 51,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 26,
                        "end": 26
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "start": 52,
                    "end": 52,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 22,
                        "end": 22
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 53:6",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 53,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that he did no more attempt a battle with the Lamanites in that year, but he did employ his men in preparing for war, yea, and in making fortifications to guard against the Lamanites, yea, and also delivering their women and their children from famine and affliction, and providing food for their armies.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 53:7",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 53,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And now it came to pass that the armies of the Lamanites, on the west sea, south, while in the absence of Moroni on account of some intrigue amongst the Nephites, which caused dissensions amongst them, had gained some ground over the Nephites, yea, insomuch that they had obtained possession of a number of their cities in that part of the land.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 176,
            "end": 187,
            "text": "Alma 31:8; Hel. 1:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 31:8; Hel. 1:15.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 31:8; Helaman 1:15",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 31,
                    "end": 31,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 8,
                        "end": 8
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "helaman",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 1,
                    "end": 1,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 15,
                        "end": 15
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 53:8",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 53,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And thus because of iniquity amongst themselves, yea, because of dissensions and intrigue among themselves they were placed in the most dangerous circumstances.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "Josh. 7:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Josh. 7:4.",
            "prettyString": "Joshua 7:4",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "joshua",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 7,
                    "end": 7,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 4,
                        "end": 4
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 53:9",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 53,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And now behold, I have somewhat to say concerning the people of Ammon, who, in the beginning, were Lamanites; but by Ammon and his brethren, or rather by the power and word of God, they had been converted unto the Lord; and they had been brought down into the land of Zarahemla, and had ever since been protected by the Nephites.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "Alma 27:26."
          },
          {
            "start": 195,
            "end": 204,
            "text": "Alma 23:13 (8–13)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 27:26.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 27:26",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 27,
                    "end": 27,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 26,
                        "end": 26
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 53:10",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 53,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And because of their oath they had been kept from taking up arms against their brethren; for they had taken an oath that they never would shed blood more; and according to their oath they would have perished; yea, they would have suffered themselves to have fallen into the hands of their brethren, had it not been for the pity and the exceeding love which Ammon and his brethren had had for them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 126,
            "end": 131,
            "text": "Alma 24:18 (17–19)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 53:11",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 53,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And for this cause they were brought down into the land of Zarahemla; and they ever had been protected by the Nephites.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 102,
            "text": "Alma 27:23."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 27:23.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 27:23",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 27,
                    "end": 27,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 23,
                        "end": 23
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 53:12",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 53,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "But it came to pass that when they saw the danger, and the many afflictions and tribulations which the Nephites bore for them, they were moved with compassion and were desirous to take up arms in the defence of their country.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "TG Affliction; Tribulation."
          },
          {
            "start": 168,
            "end": 176,
            "text": "Alma 24:18 (17–19); 56:7."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Affliction; Tribulation.",
            "prettyString": "TG Affliction; TG Tribulation",
